0..71 Comment "//! This fixture returns open values from a migration. Each declaration"
72..125 Comment "//! migrates to the seat and returns to the operator."
126..129 Comment "//!"
130..207 Comment "//! An open value crosses back from a migration as bytes. A crossing asks two"
208..284 Comment "//! judgements, mobility and openness. Mobility is authority. A mobile value"
285..355 Comment "//! holds nothing that means something only at the world that made it."
356..359 Comment "//!"
360..433 Comment "//! Openness is representation. An open value names no location. So every"
434..510 Comment "//! world reads its bytes the same way. The two judgements agree on data and"
511..588 Comment "//! part at a handle. A handle is always mobile, and open when its content is"
589..598 Comment "//! open."
599..602 Comment "//!"
603..663 Comment "//! - cites: [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]"
664..667 Comment "//!"
668..835 Comment "//! [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-78663-4_9 \"Murphy, Crary and Harper, Type-Safe Distributed Programming with ML5\""
